                                <strong style="color:#000;">Remark :</strong>
                                <span>VISA INFORMATION AS BELOW FOR KAZAKHSTAN

Please note 
* Pakistani Nationals will require *LOI + Visit to Embassy/Consulate to travel to Kazakhstan - STICKER VISA

 Pakistani Nationals are required to obtain a Letter of Invitation (LOI) before visiting the Consulate/Embassy. The LOI approval process has no guaranteed time limit and may take an extended period 

For nationalities requiring STICKER VISA once the LOI is approved, guests must book an appointment with the Embassy/Consulate of Kazakhstan. As securing an appointment can take additional time, we kindly request that you plan the travel schedule and document submission accordingly to avoid any delays.

The guests may need LOI + E-Visa or LOI + Visit the Embassy/Consulate for STICKER VISA as per the nationalities please refer the below website to check the visa requirements

https://egov.kz/cms/en/articles/for_foreigners/visa_regime_for_foreigners

https://egov.kz/cms/en/articles/rk_visa_obtaining

Guests will require a Letter of Invitation (LOI) to apply for an E-VISA We can assist in obtaining the LOI and arranging the E-Visa.

All nationals requiring a E-VISA OR a STICKER VISA will have to get an approved LOI.
Consulate/Embassy will not issue a Visa without an approved LOI.
KAZIN DMC, your trusted and reliable partner will assist with LOI.
Time taken 15 working days (if approved by authorities)

Documents Required
* A colored copy of your passport
* Date of travel
* Your Permanent/Home Country address
* Your Work/Current address
* Photograph with a white background
* A copy of your resident permit or Govt ID (if applicable)
* The place where you will be applying for the visa

Once the Letter of Intent (LOI) is approved, its validity typically ranges from 40 to 90 days, as specified on the LOI

Once converted to an E-visa or Sticker Visa travel must be completed in 30 Days.

Cost: LOI only - U$ 60/- Per Person

The above rates are valid only if packages are arranged through Kazin DMC.

If packages are not done with us, in addition to the above charges a fee of $120/- Per Person will be applicable

 LOI approvals are subject to Government/Immigration approvals 

There will be no refunds issued in case of any rejections

Please be advised of the following validity periods regarding the visa process for Kazakhstan:

  - Letter of Invitation (LOI): Once the Letter of Intent (LOI) is approved, its validity typically ranges from 40 to 90 days, as specified on the LOI
  - E-visa or Sticker Visa: Once the LOI is converted into an E-visa or a Sticker Visa, travel must be completed within 30 days.</span>
